      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$s_1=\\frac12\\times\\frac{10}{3}\\times3^2=15$ and $v=\\frac{10}{3}\\times3=10$ — B1 FT. Distance $s_1$ in 3 s and $v$ after 3 s; FT $a$ from (b).\n\n$-0.3g\\sin\\theta-\\mu\\times0.3g\\cos\\theta=0.3a$ leading to $a=-10$; $0=10^2+2(-10)s_2$ — M1. Apply Newton’s second law after 4 N removed, find $a$ and use $v^2=u^2+2as$ to find extra distance $s_2$.\n\n[$s_2=5$, leading to total distance $s_1+s_2=15+5=20\\text{ m}$] — A1.\n\nAlternative method for Question 7(c):\n\nWork done $=4\\times\\frac12\\times\\frac{10}{3}\\times3^2$ $[=60\\text{ J}]$ — B1 FT. WD $=Fs$ and $s=\\frac12at^2$ for 4 N force; FT $a$ from (b).\n\n$60=\\mu\\times0.3g\\cos\\theta\\times d+0.3g\\times d\\sin\\theta$ — M1. Balance the work done by the 4 N force against work done against $F$ and the PE gain.\n\n$d=20\\text{ m}$ — A1.\n\nTotal: 3",
